# Needed for exactly one package.
#
# @achrinza/node-ipc — a transitive dependency of @vue/cli-service's dev server
# — declares `engines.node` as an ENUMERATION ending at 19, so it refuses to
# install on anything newer even though it runs fine. It is unmaintained, and
# nothing else in the tree has an upper bound.
#
# This flag is blunt: it silences engine checks for EVERY package, so it can
# also hide a real incompatibility. Delete it the day the Vue CLI dev server
# goes away or node-ipc is dropped upstream, and re-run a clean install to check
# what it was covering. Same call, and same caveat, as the Cinema Roll repo.
--ignore-engines true
